==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
At the start of the battle, spam meatshields to prevent enemies from hitting your base and level up your wallet. Once the Shy Boys appear, spam your heavy hitters and back them up with meatshields. Don't worry, the Shy Boys are the main threats here, and they have only 300% strength magnification (100% less than in [[Twin Peaks]]), so they should be easy to stall and kill. Make sure to kill them before One Horn reaches your cats, or else they will protect the Shy Boys and attack your meatshields, making the battle harder. If you do so, you've already won this stage.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The main threat in this stage is a Bore, but it does not spawn until the base is hit. As such, it is best to stall the beginning of the stage until you have enough money to defend against the Bore. Meatshielding alone is not enough to stop the Bore, so using [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-Controllers]] is almost required. [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]], [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]] and [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]] are greatly recommended for this purpose.

Stall out the beginning until a Shy Boy appears. On its own, it will not push very quickly, so use it as an opportunity to begin stacking attackers and Crowd-Controllers. Once you reach the base and the Bore spawns, your stack should hopefully be large enough to  prevent Bore from pushing altogether. Any [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] you may own will help with clearing the peons.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Do the same thing than in chapter 2, but bring more anti red-units to stop Bore, with the fact that the use of Pirate Cat is not recommended since it will push him and your stack will die by Maawth.

[[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Sorceress Cat]], [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Face Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] are good options for this, however don't forget to bring a good anti-alien against Maawth.

